  "preamble": "Denasalization of the open-mid nasal vowel [ɔ̃] to oral [ɔ]. In Polish, the nasal vowel ą /ɔ̃/ loses its nasality altogether before /l/ and /w/, as in the past-tense forms wziął and zaczął, just as ę becomes oral [ɛ] in the same position.",
